DESIGN DECISIONS IN THE EVENT LOOP

  Threading is enforced by the type system. Session is !Send, so the future can
  only be started with spawn_local and tokio::spawn does not compile. That is
  the D5 / section 5.3 constraint - every net-snmp call on one thread - made
  into a compile error instead of a comment. #[actix_web::main] already runs a
  current-thread runtime with a LocalSet, so no runtime of our own is needed.

  AsyncFd registrations are kept across iterations for descriptors that did not
  change. The set is still re-queried every iteration, because it changes when
  the AgentX session reconnects - that part follows FRR's agentx_events_update().
  What does NOT follow FRR is dropping and rebuilding the registration each
  time: tokio's epoll registration is edge-triggered, and recreating it on every
  wake-up can lose a readiness edge for data already sitting in the socket.
  FRR's reactor is level-triggered and does not have this problem.

  Readiness is cleared explicitly after each read. snmp_read2() drains the
  socket, so the edge is consumed; without clear_ready() the next readable()
  returns immediately and the task spins.

  If net-snmp reports neither a descriptor to watch nor a deadline, the task
  sleeps IDLE_POLL (1s) instead of blocking forever. Nothing would wake it
  otherwise, and select_all over an empty set panics.

  A failing subagent does not take the framework down. It is spawned alongside
  the HTTP service and its error is logged, not propagated. That is what makes
  this task reversible and shippable on its own.

FIRST ATTEMPT FAILED, AND FAILED SILENTLY

  Image 2026_0805_1603 was flashed and the framework never appeared as a second
  AgentX session:

    BUILD_TIME  2026_0805_1603
    ss -tnp | grep 705   ->  one session only, ISS.exe pid=300
    ps -ef               ->  app_moxa_framework pid=1228 running
    moxalog grep         ->  clean

  mx_agentx_init() never set NETSNMP_DS_AGENT_X_SOCKET, so net-snmp used its
  compiled-in default of /var/agentx/master (net-snmp-config.h:1534). snmpd on
  this product listens on tcp:127.0.0.1:705 - plugin_moxa_snmp writes that line
  into snmpd.conf at config_moxa_snmp_control.c:794.

  The failure mode is worth naming because nothing about it is visible from the
  subagent side: init_agent() returns success whether or not the address is
  reachable, and the subagent module then retries on its own alarm forever. No
  error, no log, no crash - just a session that never exists. It is only
  observable on the master.

  Fixed by making the address a parameter of mx_agentx_init(), threaded through
  Session::init() to AGENTX_SOCKET in snmp_agentx.rs, which carries the
  reference to config_moxa_snmp_control.c:794 because the two have to agree and
  nothing enforces it.

  The startup log also claimed "AgentX subagent connected", which it could not
  know. It now says "started" and names the master address.

  BUILD-ORDER TRAP, hit while fixing this: editing dl/lib_moxa_rust_snmp_agentx
  and rebuilding only app_moxa_framework compiles the framework against the OLD
  copy of the crate - the source is synced into
  output/build/lib_moxa_rust_snmp_agentx-custom only when that package itself
  is rebuilt. The failure was loud here (E0061, wrong argument count), but the
  same trap with a compatible signature change would be silent. The full chain:

    make lib_moxa_rust_snmp_agentx-rebuild \
         app_moxa_framework-rebuild \
         rust_moxa_build-rebuild

